  "id": "drug-self-administration",
  "term": "drug self-administration",
  "definition": "Drug self-administration is a research method in which subjects obtain an addictive drug through their own behavior, allowing investigators to study behavioral, neurobiological, and genetic aspects of addiction. In this context, measures such as drug-taking responses and locomotor activity can be examined as related but distinct indicators.",
